  "fields": {
    "title": "Code Editor",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "To code a website by hand, you don't necessary need a code editor, you can also use a simple text editor, but it is quite useful to use a code editor, especially for beginners. Nowadays, code editors  can do more than just capture and save text. Most offer syntax highlighting, which improves readability, auto-completion and code folding, which enhances clarity and management. They also usually include very flexible search/replace tools, as well as regular expressions. Git integration for version management and flexible customisation of the editor, such as choosing a colour theme or installing extensions, are also very useful. An extremely helpful extension for any code editor is ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "uri": "https://github.com/features/copilot"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "Github Copilot",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ", which is a cloud-based artificial intelligence tool that helps you code through completion and suggestions. Other great extensions and setting are e.g. Emmett, Prettier, LiveServer, GitLens, markdownlint and Format On Save. Some code editors like visual studio code let you also access the ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "5xxqnW1VsVWs2TSUh1pSzE",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "terminal",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " from inside their interface. ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Did you know that you can take a look at the source code of every Website on the Internet? This is possible by opening the ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "3kpgl4hPVcbTfdNGnwPfUJ",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "Dev Tools",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " in your browser. Of course you don't need a Code Editor and coding skills to build a website these days, there are also a lot of ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "7gVQobWbxFti05whwYInu5",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "no-code editors",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " on the internet.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Background",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "The first code editor probably was LEXX by Mike Cowlishaw of IBM in 1985, which used live parsing and colour syntax highlighting.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
